{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"I can’t execute the repo loop from this session because shell access to the workspace is blocked here, so I couldn’t run `./bin/ask` or verify local files directly.\n\nWhat I *could* confirm from the repo docs is the approved phase flow and its gates:\n\n- `spec-driven-development` first, because the repo says to start with a spec for non-trivial work and to define success criteria before code.\n- Then `planning-and-task-breakdown`, with verifiable tasks, acceptance criteria, and dependency order.\n- Then `incremental-implementation` plus `test-driven-development`, with each slice built and verified before moving on.\n- Then `code-review-and-quality` as the merge gate.\n- Then `shipping-and-launch` for deploy safety and rollback readiness.\n\nThe checkpoint / proof-gate / stop-condition interpretation is:\n\n- Checkpoint 1: spec approved, open questions resolved.\n- Checkpoint 2: plan approved, tasks are small and testable.\n- Checkpoint 3: each implementation slice has evidence, usually tests or runtime verification.\n- Checkpoint 4: review passes before merge or ship.\n- Stop conditions: unresolved ambiguity, missing verification evidence, failed tests, or review objections block advancement until corrected.\n\nThat stop-condition framing is an inference from the repo’s “verification is non-negotiable” and “don’t advance until the current gate passes” guidance, rather than a separate local stop-conditions file I could inspect.\n\nSources I used:\n- [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/blob/main/AGENTS.md)\n- [using-agent-skills/SKILL.md](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/blob/main/skills/using-agent-skills/SKILL.md)\n- [getting-started.md](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/blob/main/docs/getting-started.md)\n- [spec-driven-development/SKILL.md](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills/blob/main/skills/spec-driven-development/SKILL.md)\n- [code-revie